{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss","id":1382610,"title":"Two Baali Theories, lets discuss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-19T15:35:22-07:00","id":1382610,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Two Baali Theories, lets discuss","content":"So normally people go with the assumed three progenitor Baali embraced by an Antediluvian named Ashur, who was implied to be either Saulot as a gamble in the Jyhad or a mistake, or Cappadocius as Ashur is a reference to his geographical namesake. We got an apocryphal tale of Haquim embracing a shepherd boy with a fated damnation to shepherd the Baali into a form that could be fought. Later we got an account of Tzimisce slaying the First Tribe and siring the Baali, and also the idea Ashur is the name of the site of the Baali rather then the Ante who sired them. Last we got from Beckett's investigations the idea Ashur was the state Antediluvians went into when giving into their Beast.<br /> <br /> So I bring up the idea we discuss two theories not often discussed. First that the Baali instead of being a Bloodline of the Antediluvians are the Children of their own Antediluvian, suggested to either be Namtaru, or the being sleeping in the Coffin labelled Nergal in the Ghost of Enoch. This could be interesting to explore, and it could explain why they were so hard to snuff out by the Cainite's of old.<br /> <br /> The 2nd theory is instead of the Baali being sired by a single Antediluvian, or my personal theory of three (merging the accounts of Haquim, Tzimisce, and Zao-lat as all being true), that instead they were sired by the entire Antediluvian Host at the time. This would mean maybe 13 original Baali 4th gens at the time, and the traditional 3 Baali fathers could represent just the ones that survived past the ages of antiquity. This holds some promising story potential, like maybe why Moloch and Troile were lovers was because they were both Sired by Ilyes and had many shared pains and regrets. The Assamite Revised clanbook certainly makes it seem like there were a ton of 4th gen, considering Haquim who was charged with culling the unwanted illicitly sired Cainites himself sired well over a dozen in those ancient nights of yore.<br /> <br /> <br /> And with this idea I wonder, could it be possible Ur-Shulgi doesn't have a Beast, if Haquim plucked the demon possessing him out of his burning form. I personally like the idea of Ur-Shulgi being a Ferectoi, a child born a fomor, but he could have just been a child possessed by a spirit, or more popularly suggested by fans is the idea he was a Widderslant mage. But I like to think when possessed spirits bind and root into a beings lower soul, and its intriguing to consider how Ur-Shulgi possibly going from Baali to Banu Haquim because he had his Demon removed, or that removing the Demon gripping strongly into his beast caused Ur-Shulgi to be so cold and calculating because he is only a Hun souled vessel. <br /> <br /> But these present a lot of seldom discussed options.<br /> <br /> If the Baali were from a true Baali Antediluvian I would have it that this being's 2nd Generation progenitor was in fact Apep, as it fits with the idea that a Mysterious being named Typhon Embraced Osiris and maybe Osiris was also a 3rd Gen who never embraced rather then a 4th gen. Sutekh was said to have diablerized Apep, a being normally considered a Demon/Neverborn/Wyrm. But it could be interesting if this was some sort of Dark Apotheosis for this being and it became the entity it is now in a similar fashion that Cappadocius tried to accomplish by having his childe eat him while his soul escaped, or how Lasombra faked his demise, and maybe even had his body destroyed so he could become a being of the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:52:18-07:00","id":1382635,"title":"","content":"You've certainly connected some dots in a different way that I usually do, and I like that a lot. You've put some time and thought into adding your own creativity to the gaps in the lore, something that more World of Darkness fans should feel free to do.<br /> <br /> Here's one argument in favor of the plausibility of the Baali coming from an otherwise unknown Antedeluvian: they have Obfuscate as a clan discipline, and one suggested power for rank 10 Obfuscate from an old Vampire supplement is the ability to remove oneself completely from history, disappearing from the memory of everyone in the world. Obviously, we don't know of any character who has ever done this, which might as well be proof that the power works.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi being a monster from another game line before his embrace may or may not be problematic depending on how much you want the mythologies and lores of other game lines to cross over into your Vampire game. As someone who gravitated very strongly to the end-of-the-world/Y2K hysteria of Vampire 3rd Edition, I believe that Ur-Shulgi's primary importance to the story was that his conduct showed his ancient sire's attitude to the modern clan and its culture. Ur-Shulgi's lethal hostility to the clan's embrace of Abrahamic faiths, in particular, comes across as a dire warning when taken in the context of the lore and mythology specific to the world of Vampire. That well full of Haqim's blood form in the clan's mountain stronghold sounds far too much like a Baali worship site to be a coincidence, and I believe that Haqim has been playing a very, very long game. The appeal of this theory, to me, is partly that it works with just Vampire lore tools, without any addons or plug-ins from other game lines needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T17:42:56-07:00","id":1382642,"title":"","content":"The thing about Obfuscate 10 is a great point, as is the Well of Blood being compared to a Baali Pit of Sacrifice!<br /> <br /> Yeah it was broadly described about Ur-Shulgi having a damned soul so you don't need to dip into other gamelines, though one could argue things like Sorcerers and Fomori (basically demon possessed) are kind of cross gameline elements already, and The House of Haquim already tied much of their history to fighting Demons and to embracing Sorcerers and Mages, not just Al-Ashrad but Haquim embraced a buttload of magic wisemen to help brainstorm his nascent Sorcerer Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T17:43:14-07:00","id":1382643,"title":"","content":"Some Baali theories of my own:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Baali are a fuck up, not a master plan</b>: The original story of the Baali was Ashur Embracing them in a fit of pique rather than as part of a 3-dimensional Jyhad stroke. My view is that this actually is more interesting than the &quot;Antes being super-geniuses in all things.&quot; Saulot Embraced a bunch of Infernalists to show them what real evil was because he viewed his condition as a curse and was disgusted by what they were up to. The problem was that he created a bunch of 4th generation super-beings as a result because not everyone will view vampirism through his Sad LouisTM attitude. So he spent something like the next 8000 years hunting them down with Haqim.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Ur-Shulgi is a brainwashed Baali</b>: I generally go with the idea that the 3 Baali are Ur-Shulgi, Moloch, and Shaitan. My idea is Ur-Shulgi was grabbed by Haqim, brainwashed, and promptly set upon his fellows by the others. I actually think Ur-Shulgi is sincere in his desire to purge his fellow infernalists (as much as someone can be sincere after an Ante wipes their brain and soul clean with Blood Sorcery as well as Dominate). However, it adds an interesting new perspective to the idea that he hates Islam and other religions among the Banu Haqim because he'd be tortured by it as a Baali. He still has the Clan Flaw of being repulsed by religious symbols after all and Clan Flaws get worse not better the more powerful you become.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The True Hand is subverted by Moloch and Troile</b>: The True Hand uncharacteristically accepting the Baali into their ranks strikes me as very likely that they are brainwashed by a powerful force in the Jyhad that more or less wiped their minds of better sense. My view for maximum humor value is that Moloch and Troile are the parties responsible. The current Del Rol is, in fact, the female Antediluvian of the Brujah that is more bemused than anything else at the ridiculousness of the &quot;True Brujah.&quot; Either way, the Baali have effectively taken the True Hand and its resources into its ranks and allow the Bloodline access to its previous levels of power.<br /> <br /> The big irony being the True Hand's most ludicrous and quixotic quest of fighting &quot;Soul Eaters&quot; (misunderstood banes) is something the Baali actually approve of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:45:40-07:00","id":1382751,"title":"","content":"Usually it's assumed that Saulot sired the three original Baali (Nergal, Moloch and the Unnamed). Ashur as the Baali progenitor was first considered during the Vampire the Dark Ages era (back in '98). V20 changed that to ur-Shulgi somehow being that third one (an idea I heavily dislike).<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Namtaru being the progenitor of the bloodline and antediluvian, curse by Caine to never sire childer. Due to this he learned from beyond entities to re-embrace cainites from other clans so perhaps Nergal from the Cappadocian and Moloch from the Salubri could have been their chosen for the re-embrace in order to have that more than one antediluvian sire for the original three. Back in the day, before Clanbook Baali, it was believed that Shaitan was the first and there was one Baali who abandoned their antediluvian sire from each clan (Dark Ages Companion '97) so that can suit better the several clan progenitor's theory.<br /> <br /> The Eldest being a sire for Baali is something I can't consider. He stole or learned his magic from a demon bound to the carpathians and his pursue of azhi dahaka is enough already for the need to include even more infernal origins beyond what they already know from Koldunic Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I never like the idea of ur-Shulgi being more than a really powerful 4th generation sorcerer. Him being embraced through a weird process involving infernal I can understand and the justification of this being Haqim desiring to destroy the Baali from within is an interesting concept. To speculate even further beyond this is something I really can't follow, involving Werewolf spirit physiology is beyond my comprehension.<br /> <br /> On Set, it's kind of too much to think of him as a former 4th generation diablerizing his sire. On Troile (anger one) is an idea that was formed since the beginning and it is an accepted concept in the mythos of Vampire, but having Set being similar (though different due to involving other games mechanics) is something I wouldn't agree on. When it comes to [Lasombra] apotheosis I'll quote a phrase in Gehenna that I liked &quot;whatever is in the abyss, it isn't a Cainite anymore&quot;<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:24:19-07:00","id":1382775,"title":"","content":"1. Ur-Shulgi being the third Baali is something that I think is interesting because there's a connection between the Children of Haqim and the Baali that rarely gets mentioned. The two clans were archenemies long before the Salubri and the Baali were. We also note that Ur-Shulgi has a charcoal skin cover for his features while his only known child has lily-white skin. This was more of a thing before the Banu Haqim were retconned as not turning coal black as they aged (perhaps to avoid racial implications).<br /> <br /> 2. A good Antediluvian for Embracing the Baali alternative would be Malkav. Set embracing the Baali feels like a flanderization of his character since they embody corruption but it's a tool to enlightenment not an end to their own sake. Ventrue is an interesting optional twist as Tiamat and other vampires of his lineage pretended to be gods as well as engaged in infernalism.<br /> <br /> 3. Some people have speculated that Shaitan may not actually be a Baali founder at all. Aside from the fact that he's one of the Baali that does want to destroy the world and he looks like an enormous goat-monster from all his Infernal investments, he could be a vampire that was converted from his previous Clan to being a Baali.<br /> <br /> 4. I've sometimes speculated that Troile was sired by Ventrue and that the True Brujah are missing that vital information. That would mean that the Ventrue and Brujah are brother and sister clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T13:19:02-07:00","id":1382817,"title":"","content":"I have previously posted my <u>head canon</u> on the subject of the Baali origins <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/956942-does-my-discipline-have-to-be-evil-diamonion-vicissitude-etc\">here</a>, down in post 6.<br /> <br /> I reprint it here for simplicity sake:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine you're in Enoch, the Second City, or just Ye Olde Hyborean Age back in the day. There's all kinds of crazy stuff going on: cannibal cults, demon worship, Cthulhu summoning, shape shifting soul eating plagues, defiling of sacred temples, cats sleeping with dogs... real Sodom and Gemorrah stuff.<br /> <br /> Caine, or maybe an unnamed Antedeluvian, looks around and says, &quot;Hmmm, this is getting out of hand. I should create a sort of morality secret police to tamp down the worst excesses. They need to be sneaky to infiltrate the doomsday cults, but also charismatic enough to lead the usual torch wielding band of moralists. Let's have a specialty discipline that detects evil, convinces people it's the wrong thing to do, blasts the unrepentant, forces anyone who survives that to battle their own inner demons and, then, finally, levies a judgment against the guilty in the form of a curse. Let's name the line after the local legitimate deities that have respectable, established religions so the common folk will accept their moral authority.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's my guess at the origin of the Baali.<br /> <br /> Of course, after a while the narcs always wind up sampling from the evidence locker and it all goes south, which brings us the modern Baali. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:01:59-07:00","id":1382822,"title":"","content":"Ironically, Malkav and Haqim are exactly the sort of Antediluvians who would also Embrace the Baali as a punishment.<br /> <br /> Set might have Embraced them because he thought they were poseurs.<br /> <br /> Lasombra because he is the kind of guy who might have actually wanted to bring about the end of the world.<br /> <br /> Ravnos could have done it because destroying this incarnation of reality would result in the next cycle of the Wheel.<br /> <br /> A more arcane or interesting motivation could be Ashur/Cappadocius embracing them so they could incarnate evil and give the Kindred something worse than themselves to fight against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:14:32-07:00","id":1382823,"title":"","content":"Hmm I probably could have been clearer, I was particularly interested in discussing the Two theories that normally I don't use, the idea they had an Actual Ante and the idea that maybe their were a lot more then 3 Original Baali. Though I am also interested in other ideas that are new an unused.<br /> <br /> But I was curious as to good hooks to use these two ideas.<br /> <br /> Also I get more and more of a feeling their really should have been more then 13 Antes, because that way we can have stories of Ante Rivals and Antes being destroyed, with the 13 clans being the Survivors.<br /> <br /> One idea I am playing with is Baali could have by default been the Caitiff of the 2nd city, because nonkosher Embraces were punished by slaying the Sire and Childe, Caitiff are left with joining the only group that would have them, the ones already hunted, and even the non Infernal Caitiff are treated as if they are demons anyways.<br /> <br /> Its really Curious how Mastery of Daimonion could Manifest since Daimonion 9 already makes you a Vessel for Beings that could rival Caine.<br /> <br /> But even if Ur-Shulgi wasn't Baali at one point his backstory seems to really blur the line of Demon Worship and God Worship since even back in the 2nd City he and his Peers seemed to be worshipped as bloody terrible gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:19:58-07:00","id":1382824,"title":"","content":"And also there is the discussion of Azrael-Caine in the Talmaherah Book where Caine and Lilith needed to work together to make the 2nd Gen, so they can't really make anymore because they had a falling out.<br /> <br /> And of course the many Stories of Lilith's children being rivals to the Antes, and eventually betrayed and Murdered by them, but also of the ideas some of her Children became Antes or were in some form of hostage exchange where she traded some of her kids for Caines.<br /> <br /> Lilith seemed to be the Snake in the Garden of Eden, and possibly even the one who impregnated Eve with Caine. I could see Lilith possibly secretly being Apep through this connection, especially with the ideas brought up in the Analects of the 3rd Garden where she was the Queen of the Abyss and a fragment of Ialdeboath's reincarnation. The Baali then could be her Children. Or maybe the actual Children (the beings that seem to be the sleeping Corpses of the Neverborn in the Mortal World) are her Children, or the fragments of Ialderboath that got knocked into slumber during the big Let There Be Light'ening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T16:46:50-07:00","id":1382847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss?p=1382823#post1382823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm I probably could have been clearer, I was particularly interested in discussing the Two theories that normally I don't use, the idea they had an Actual Ante and the idea that maybe their were a lot more then 3 Original Baali. Though I am also interested in other ideas that are new an unused.<br /> <br /> But I was curious as to good hooks to use these two ideas.<br /> <br /> Also I get more and more of a feeling their really should have been more then 13 Antes, because that way we can have stories of Ante Rivals and Antes being destroyed, with the 13 clans being the Survivors.<br /> <br /> One idea I am playing with is Baali could have by default been the Caitiff of the 2nd city, because nonkosher Embraces were punished by slaying the Sire and Childe, Caitiff are left with joining the only group that would have them, the ones already hunted, and even the non Infernal Caitiff are treated as if they are demons anyways.<br /> <br /> Its really Curious how Mastery of Daimonion could Manifest since Daimonion 9 already makes you a Vessel for Beings that could rival Caine.<br /> <br /> But even if Ur-Shulgi wasn't Baali at one point his backstory seems to really blur the line of Demon Worship and God Worship since even back in the 2nd City he and his Peers seemed to be worshipped as bloody terrible gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always like the idea of having more than 13 Antediluvians, that was one of the only strong points of Gehenna book (though having them all in Fair is Foul scenario wasn't). Second City's Caitiff being the Baali could be the source of the &quot;Caitiff can create disciplines&quot; therefore the reason on why Daimoinon max out at 9. On Open the Way level 9 power, I always thought of it more of a Second City Blood Sorcery (or Dark proto-Thaumaturgy) level 9 ritual more than being Daimoinon level 9. Perhaps there can be more options for that level of power than we know of.<br /> <br /> The being that enters reality through Daimoinon level 9 might rival Caine in power but I doubt that it can actually kill him (God's curse is too OP). Caine wasn't THAT powerful back then, it was Lilith that taught him how to use his own power, so perhaps she knows more about those beings than Caine or the Baali does.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:55:57-07:00","id":1382861,"title":"","content":"God's curse is more a deterrent rather then an Aegis. And that more applies if say its Fallen Angel style Demons, if its something Abrahamic like Apep/Wyrm/Cthulhoid then I don't see why they would be automatically check mated by a deities edict. Everyone tries to say you can't break the Curse of Caine because you can't roll more successes then god, but that is not quite nuanced enough for. After all Osiris removed the Curse of Caine on multiple vampires at once, he was also a God. Vampire only has stories about omnipotence, it doesn't provide incontrovertible truths about God. After all considering at least Two Antes believe they can take God's Throne, and that Throne is also recognized by the Middle Kingdom as the Throne of Heaven and of a different type of God then the Cainites ascribe cursed Adam. And from the point of view of Lilith Caine isn't cursed by the Omnipotent Alpha of the Universe, she had it that Jehovah was just one of many Elohim, and Eden was his Garden, Ra had another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T18:27:33-07:00","id":1382866,"title":"","content":"Crossover chronicles have interesting implications for Lilith.<br /> <br /> None of the Fallen's firsthand accounts of Eden, in any of the published D:tF books, mention her being there at all.<br /> <br /> If she exists, she could be something entirely different from what she's mythologized herself as being. The mother of demons, who wars against the children of Caine, could easily be retconned as an early generation Baali or even their creator if it suits you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T18:48:32-07:00","id":1382870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss?p=1382866#post1382866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover chronicles have interesting implications for Lilith.<br /> <br /> None of the Fallen's firsthand accounts of Eden, in any of the published D:tF books, mention her being there at all.<br /> <br /> If she exists, she could be something entirely different from what she's mythologized herself as being. The mother of demons, who wars against the children of Caine, could easily be retconned as an early generation Baali or even their creator if it suits you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting viewpoint! I always was let down that they never mentioned Lilith but I never considered what if she wasn't the first Wife of Adam? And she faked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:14:00-07:00","id":1382874,"title":"","content":"What if the three original Baali (Nergal, Moloch and the Unnamed) were not all Sired by the same Ante?<br /> <br /> I think Troile and Moloch were lovers (this works regardless of Troile\u2019s gender), but that\u2019s just my headcanon.<br /> <br /> What did Lilith fake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:24:29-07:00","id":1382876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss?p=1382874#post1382874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the three original Baali (Nergal, Moloch and the Unnamed) were not all Sired by the same Ante?<br /> <br /> I think Troile and Moloch were lovers (this works regardless of Troile\u2019s gender), but that\u2019s just my headcanon.<br /> <br /> What did Lilith fake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes posted that theory in the beginning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, with the Unnamed being Haquim's kid, Tzimisce and Salubri both embracing Nergal and Moloch out of spite. I took the whole they tossed the tribe into the pit and spit blood at their corpses as the moment they were Embraced, I even think they might not of intended to embrace them but the unwholesome magic of the Pit of Ashur caused the blood they spit into the pit to embrace them.<br /> <br /> Reasor was suggesting a possible reason that Lilith wasn't known to the Fallen was because she may have came afterwards and made up her origins as a Pre Cain player on the world stage. Its certainly an idea I never considered. It could work well with say the theory she is the Crone, so maybe she was an old witch who taught Caine the Blood Bond, blood bonded him but was staked for the sun. I believe Gehenna gives the idea that the Crone was the 2nd wife of Adam, the one after Lilith who Adam was grossed out seeing made from clay, so God banished her and made Eve from his rib.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:40:14-07:00","id":1382880,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Fallen don\u2019t mention Lilith because they didn\u2019t like her (either because she overshadowed Lucifer during the Fall of Eden or because the other Fallen resented how close she and Lucifer were). I don\u2019t think Lilith and the Crone were literally the same person (the Crone is very old and the Midrashim describes Lilith as being young and vigorous), but maybe they\u2019re two aspects of the same being.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not an expert on the Baali, but I agree with the points you made in your original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:52:35-07:00","id":1382883,"title":"","content":"My going idea is in I believe Houses of the Fallen, the same book that seems to describe the Lasombra Abyss was a network of shadows they made rather then their prison the Abyss, they talk about a lot of their secrets about the Early Creation was removed from their mind and given to Lucifer and they don't know everything that that even gave him. So that fits for me all the Animism and Lilith stuff.<br /> <br /> The Crone to me seemed like a parable retelling of Caine and Lilith retold when Caine was King rather then a nomad and with Zillah rather then Lilith as the beautiful being that enraptured him. There is also Talk that Lilith has probably Maiden Mother and Crone aspects that she has taken.<br /> <br /> But I really like the idea that Lilith was the Snake in the Garden of Eden rather then Lucifer. After all the conflating of the Serpent and Satan happened much later in history, just like the conflating of several of the Mary's in Jesus' life into only two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T20:15:04-07:00","id":1382886,"title":"","content":"I think Lilith as the Crone is just Lilith being shapeshifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T21:14:14-07:00","id":1382897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss?p=1382886#post1382886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lilith as the Crone is just Lilith being shapeshifted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This does remind me of Mithras and Kemintiri in Victorian Age trilogy, when the Setite posed as &quot;Daeva&quot; to get Noushad against his sire-to-be Mithras.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T21:28:09-07:00","id":1382898,"title":"","content":"I guess Lilith and Kemintiri are kind of similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T22:16:46-07:00","id":1382902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss?p=1382861#post1382861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone tries to say you can't break the Curse of Caine because you can't roll more successes then god, but that is not quite nuanced enough for. After all Osiris removed the Curse of Caine on multiple vampires at once, he was also a God.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that being due to a workaround even if Osiris isn't able to overcome Yahweh's works directly. It's certainly within the power of a god to break the Curse of Caine the simplest way, by <i>killing</i> a bunch of vampires. And once they're truly dead, well, guess who just happens to be a god of the afterlife and resurrection who said vampires worship? He'd naturally be the one to determine what happens to their souls once they've died.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T22:30:39-07:00","id":1382904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1382610-two-baali-theories-lets-discuss?p=1382902#post1382902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that being due to a workaround even if Osiris isn't able to overcome Yahweh's works directly. It's certainly within the power of a god to break the Curse of Caine the simplest way, by <i>killing</i> a bunch of vampires. And once they're truly dead, well, guess who just happens to be a god of the afterlife and resurrection who said vampires worship? He'd naturally be the one to determine what happens to their souls once they've died.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha that is clever! I mean he did just leave the unworthy as ashes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T02:10:55-07:00","id":1382931,"title":"","content":"Which of the Two Theories (that either Baali had an actual Antediluvian and are therefore a clan, or that all or almost all Antediluvians sired a Baali so there were at least 13 Baali 4th Gen in the days of yore).<br /> <br /> <br /> I would point out since the Baali were already marked for death nothing really stopped them from siring and siring so they would probably even be the first Group that had high Generation childer. So they are lead by 4th gen, they could sire indiscriminately when at war, and their 5th Gen can go farther and Sire 6th Gen and they sire 7th. I wonder what the limit was back then? Maybe 8th gen? Or 7th Gen?<br /> <br /> It would be so degenerate and odd since most of the 2nd city think 5th gen are the weak bloods, being a vampire limited by the mortal standards (8th gen limited to human level 5 traits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T06:36:17-07:00","id":1383136,"title":"","content":"Here is my theory/headcanon on the origins of the Baali:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;In the ancient nights, thousands and thousands of years ago Saulot the Kind went east in search of wisdom. So long ago was this that most of the line of Caine still dwelt in a single city. And all those millennia ago, if the Antediluvians had no human hearts, they were still closer to them than today. Especially Saulot, who strove to retain as much of a heart as he could.<br /> <br /> Saulot walked as kine do, for it was a pilgrimage. For many nights he walked through dry, empty lands where men were scarce or altogether absent. But one night he heard a song, the most beautiful he ever head. And Saulot followed the song through the sand and the rock and he came to a city. Green and fertile and strewn with lights it was, and Saulot thought it beautiful. And for a while he tarried there and sought the singer whose song he had followed. Time and perhaps other things have obscured the name of the place. Some say it was called Ashur, some say Ubar of the Pit.<br /> <br /> But Saulot found the singer. Rayzeel, a slave in that city. And Saulot fell in love and stayed for long years in that place. Freedom and much favor came upon Rayzeel as the consort of the Antediluvian. Saulot gave wealth, and comfort, magic and the wisdom of ages. But Saulot withheld from his consort one thing: Immortality and the blood of Caine. For he saw its immortality through murder as a curse, not a gift. In the end, Saulot continued his pilgrimage east, promising to return when his quest was complete.<br /> <br /> And Rayzeel wept, still mortal and considering that betrayal.<br /> <br /> In the end, Saulot completed his quest. He gained great wisdom, and entered into the state of Golconda. And he returned to that city, for the Antediluvian truly did love Rayzeel the Singer, beyond all other beings. But this time he did not hear song as he approached, he could follow the sound of screams. And he saw Rayzeel standing above the pit, and he saw what his love had done with the knowledge he had given. For Rayzeel had seen immortality up close, touched it, and knew that it was possible through blood and murder. And so all the power and favor that was given Rayzeel had been turned to the task. The first organ-pit grew in the heart of the city, and Rayzeel stood above it, crimson with blood and making a chorus of the victims screams.<br /> <br /> Saulot saw his love so, and Saulot fell.<br /> <br /> First in Golconda, he time in that state was the shortest of all who have held it. In frenzy he tore through the people, victims and perpetrators alike. Their broken, twisted and exsanguinated bodies he threw into the pit, and Rayzeel he left for last. And even that last plea did not move him &quot;I did it for you. To live until you returned&quot; His love went last into the pit.<br /> <br /> On the edge of the pit Saulot awoke from frenzy and realized all he had lost. Love, wisdom and golconda were all dust. And the Antediluvian fell to his knees and wept like rain. As he knelt on the brink, he sobbed forth words that have echoed down the ages to follow the kindred until they have been mistaken for Caines own words:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Do not embrace love&quot;</b><br /> <br /> And as he spoke, his bloody tears ran down into the pit, and perhaps he knew. And perhaps he didn't. For the greatest of minds can be deceived by its heart, and Saulot had labored long at retaining his heart.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 04-22-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}